WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.160
Does the Black Moon Howl?

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:04.320
No. Not yet.

00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:10.720
See the boy. He was born in a time before
names; there weren’t enough humans around

00:00:10.720 --> 00:00:17.120
to need them back then. He was one of a handful
occupying a coastal village, using a tongue

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:24.320
long since dead. They eked out a simple life
- hunting, gathering, fishing. The only thing

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:30.880
on most of their minds was surviving to see
the next sunrise. Yes, a simple life, free

00:00:30.880 --> 00:00:32.000
of complications.

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.720
Until The Hermit appeared.

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:41.120
The Boy would remember this man for an eternity.
Haggard and thin; skin weathered by time and

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:47.520
pain. A man that, emaciated, walking with
a long, gnarled cane that honestly looked

00:00:47.520 --> 00:00:53.680
healthier than he did, shouldn’t be alive.
Even the Boy, who had scarcely seen beyond

00:00:53.680 --> 00:01:00.000
the bounds of his village, knew that the Hermit
was unnatural. An aberration. An anomaly.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:06.720
He walked into the center of the village,
sat down on a large stone, and waited. Nobody

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:10.560
dared ask his business, nor what the Hermit
waited for.

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:15.520
Then, a few days later, the Black Moon howled.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:20.240
The Boy saw the village’s youngest hunter
freeze one evening while out on a walk. Not

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:27.200
simply stand still, but freeze. Then, for
an instant, he became solid black. A coal

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:33.840
statue. And as soon as he’d changed, he
was gone. Obliterated. Not a trace of him

00:01:33.840 --> 00:01:34.960
remained.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:41.200
Such is the power of the Black Moon. It can
make any conscious being disappear in an instant.

00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:47.360
Turned black, then wiped from our plane of
existence, never to be seen again. Its choice

00:01:47.360 --> 00:01:52.880
of victim seemed, at each instance, to be
utterly random, but it would come for all

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:59.120
who lived eventually. This is known to some
as the howling of the Black Moon.

00:01:59.120 --> 00:02:04.640
Later that same night, the Boy found himself
talking to the Hermit, who asked with small,

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:10.480
frantic eyes what he had seen. When the Boy
told him, he let out a deep, rattling sigh.

00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:16.560
The Boy, curious, asked him if he knew about
the nightmare he’d just witnessed. The Hermit

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:21.680
looked up. He’d been the first one, in the
Hermit’s millennia of pursuit, that had

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:27.920
ever asked. In that moment, he knew he had
found his successor in the hunt for the Death

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:28.960
of Ages.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:35.600
The Hermit told the Boy it went by many names.
The Great Finale, the Pale King, but most

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:42.000
common of all was the Black Moon. The entity
existed beyond the veil of our reality, a

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:48.240
creature of pure energy, though nobody could
really be sure of its true nature. The Hermit

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:54.400
had been tracking it, learning about it, and
trying to destroy it for thousands of years.

00:02:54.400 --> 00:02:59.920
And yet, it only took him four pathetic minutes
to tell the Boy everything he knew.

00:02:59.920 --> 00:03:04.880
The Boy, knowing still that something about
the Hermit was unnatural, asked how he came

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:11.760
to be in this position. The Hermit told the
boy he was the Counterbalance, a kind of chosen

00:03:11.760 --> 00:03:17.520
one, destined to face and perhaps even defeat
the Black Moon someday. The Counterbalance

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:22.880
receives a number of truly extraordinary gifts
for inheriting the responsibility: Eternal

00:03:22.880 --> 00:03:27.280
life, eternal youth, near physical immortality.

00:03:27.280 --> 00:03:33.120
But they will be haunted by their purpose,
doomed to watch everyone they love die around

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:40.240
them, as they continue to hunt their only
true equal and opposite, the Black Moon itself.

00:03:40.240 --> 00:03:45.600
The Hermit, in his own eyes, had failed at
his duty. He had grown weary, and now, he

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:51.600
needed to pass the duty of Counterbalance
onto another. That other would be the Boy.

00:03:51.600 --> 00:03:56.400
He felt a sudden and profound change, along
with the knowledge that nothing would ever

00:03:56.400 --> 00:04:03.840
be the same again. He was no longer just the
Boy. Now, he was the Counterbalance.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:08.480
He watched the Hermit give him a slight nod
out of respect, and then crumble into dust

00:04:08.480 --> 00:04:15.440
before his eyes. The Boy, the Counterbalance,
looked up at the sky and saw the stars twinkling.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:21.680
So bright, so beautiful. Little did he know,
his battle with the Black Moon would outlast

00:04:21.680 --> 00:04:23.680
every single one of them.

00:04:23.680 --> 00:04:27.840
Does the Black Moon howl? Not without blood.

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:34.000
The Boy grew into a man, as his village aged
and then died around him. Decades passed,

00:04:34.000 --> 00:04:40.400
then centuries, then millennia. Tens of thousands
of years, watching humanity develop and grow

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:44.800
around him as he continued his pursuit of
that one elusive foe.

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.920
As science and diagnostic technology gained
ground, absorbing and then evolving beyond

00:04:49.920 --> 00:04:54.800
all the old superstitions, the Counterbalance
gained a better understanding of the Black

00:04:54.800 --> 00:05:01.680
Moon - though even then, it still remained
essentially a stranger. The entity was entropic,

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:07.600
a being of pure randomness and chaos without
consistent form. It didn’t exist in our

00:05:07.600 --> 00:05:13.040
universe, but it could exercise its influence
here with so-called “Obliteration Events”

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:18.000
- much like the horrible fate that befell
the young hunter from the village.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:21.680
But that was only the proverbial tip of the
iceberg.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:27.920
The Counterbalance tracked and noted obliteration
events. They were exceedingly rare, at first.

00:05:27.920 --> 00:05:32.960
Something that occurred once every thousand
years or so, like a terrible curse. But he

00:05:32.960 --> 00:05:35.120
couldn’t help but notice a concerning trend&nbsp;

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:38.560
emerging. It started happening&nbsp;
once a century...then

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:43.760
once a decade. He could feel the terrible
future stretching out in front of him. How,

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:49.440
over their shared eternity, the Black Moon
would gain more and more ground.

00:05:49.440 --> 00:05:55.520
Would there come a day where it took someone
once a year? One a month? A week, a day, an

00:05:55.520 --> 00:06:02.320
hour, a minute, a second? It’d spell the
end of all conscious life. A total victory

00:06:02.320 --> 00:06:09.920
for the Black Moon, the End of the Universe,
the Death of Ages. A complete existential

00:06:09.920 --> 00:06:11.120
obliteration.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:16.080
He was swept up in a sobering realization:
He couldn’t win this fight alone.

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:20.800
However, while his hunt for the Black Moon
had been largely fruitless, the Counterbalance

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:27.040
had discovered many other things along the
way, Strange creatures, objects with extraordinary

00:06:27.040 --> 00:06:32.640
powers, and events that couldn’t be explained
with rational science. Perhaps something among

00:06:32.640 --> 00:06:39.840
these oddities, these anomalies, would hold
the key to defeating his timeless enemy. And

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:45.760
it hadn’t just been these objects, entities,
and events, he’d also discovered some truly

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:51.520
exceptional people on his travels. Minds and
skills that rivaled even his own, despite

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:52.560
his age.

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:55.520
Perhaps they would be the ones to help him
win.

00:06:55.520 --> 00:07:00.320
With the thirteen most brilliant and trusted
people the Counterbalance ever met, he decided

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:06.400
to form a Council. And from this Council,
they forged and directed an organization dedicated

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:11.920
to understanding and counteracting the strange
in all its forms, with the secret hope that

00:07:11.920 --> 00:07:16.960
their search into darkness would yield the
answer to the Black Moon’s downfall.

00:07:16.960 --> 00:07:23.440
He called it the SCP Foundation. They would
Secure the anomalous, Contain it, and Protect

00:07:23.440 --> 00:07:26.560
all of humanity from its&nbsp;
influence. The Counterbalance&nbsp;

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:29.440
also took on a new title, befitting of his

00:07:29.440 --> 00:07:35.520
new role: The Administrator. And even the
Black Moon itself was given a moniker, in

00:07:35.520 --> 00:07:38.320
hopes of robbing it of some of its frightening
power.

00:07:38.880 --> 00:07:41.120
SCP-001.

00:07:41.760 --> 00:07:45.840
Does the Black Moon howl? Only at the blind.

00:07:45.840 --> 00:07:51.920
The year was now 1987. The SCP Foundation
had been operating for over a century, and

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:56.880
thanks to their secret possession of anomalous
wisdom and technology, their own advancement

00:07:56.880 --> 00:08:01.360
was thousands of years ahead of the rest of
humanity. While there still wasn’t a silver

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:06.320
bullet solution to the Black Moon, and its
deadly howls were becoming all the more frequent

00:08:06.320 --> 00:08:11.680
as the decades went on, the Foundation did
have some irons in the fire to combat it.

00:08:11.680 --> 00:08:16.480
Their ability to gather intel on both the
entity itself and its obliteration events

00:08:16.480 --> 00:08:22.160
had improved considerably, thanks to their
new global information network. Their top

00:08:22.160 --> 00:08:27.520
minds were also working on a highly classified
device known as the Singular Conceptual Bunker,

00:08:27.520 --> 00:08:33.120
which may one day come in handy for combating
the extra-dimensional entity directly. But

00:08:33.120 --> 00:08:38.000
the most valuable piece of information they
ever gathered about the Black Moon was this:

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:44.400
It couldn’t howl when it was being watched.
The very act of engaged observation defanged

00:08:44.400 --> 00:08:44.880
it.

00:08:44.880 --> 00:08:50.000
The problem is, how can you observe something
that doesn’t technically exist inside your

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:56.080
own reality? In order to pull this off, the
Foundation would need to get extremely creative.

00:08:56.080 --> 00:09:00.880
Thankfully, creative solutions to strange
problems are the Foundation’s specialty.

00:09:00.880 --> 00:09:08.000
Flash forward to 1993. Enter Dr. Moto, a brilliant
young scientist and conceptual engineer working

00:09:08.000 --> 00:09:13.920
for the SCP Foundation. With The Administrator’s
consultation, he started the KEY Project,

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:19.600
an arm of the wider Project Oromasdes - the
umbrella initiative for using modified anomalous

00:09:19.600 --> 00:09:21.840
objects in the battle against the Black Moon.

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:27.200
The goal of the KEY Project was relatively
simple: If people couldn’t observe the Black

00:09:27.200 --> 00:09:32.480
Moon directly, then the Foundation could make
proxies of the Black Moon that could be observed,

00:09:32.480 --> 00:09:37.920
almost like a kind of voodoo doll. These new
anomalies would only need to satisfy three

00:09:37.920 --> 00:09:43.680
criteria: The inability to operate when being
observed, a hostility to conscious life, and

00:09:43.680 --> 00:09:48.640
the ability to end conscious life of their
own volition when not being observed. Through

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:53.760
conceptual engineering, a link theoretically
could be forged between these objects and

00:09:53.760 --> 00:09:58.720
the Black Moon, allowing observation of them
to stop the obliteration events.

00:09:58.720 --> 00:10:03.680
However, despite being a good idea in theory,
Dr. Moto’s efforts were marred with errors

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:08.480
and tragedies. One object wasn’t deadly
enough, simply appearing behind people in

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:12.880
a threatening pose when they weren’t looking.
Another one killed purely through collateral

00:10:12.880 --> 00:10:17.440
damage - a giant sculpture of a human head
that immediately attempted escape by barging

00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:23.440
through Site-01 - the center for Anti-Black
Moon operations - and killing nineteen people

00:10:23.440 --> 00:10:29.680
in the process. Another one of Moto’s objects,
a huge black sphere, simply immediately exploded,

00:10:29.680 --> 00:10:31.120
killing twelve people.

00:10:31.120 --> 00:10:36.320
And in the most horrific misstep of all, one
of Moto’s objects caused a mass death event

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:37.840
in a nearby hotel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:37.840 --> 00:10:43.360
where 142 people were spontaneously
incinerated when the object - a series of

00:10:43.360 --> 00:10:49.760
interlocking stalactites and stalagmites - was
left unobserved for 0.2 seconds. Almost all

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.480
of Moto’s objects were terminated in the
aftermath, either being too useless or too

00:10:54.480 --> 00:10:59.920
dangerous to keep around. The young scientist
felt a deep shame, but forged on.

00:10:59.920 --> 00:11:06.240
He made one truly brilliant creation that
satisfied all the criteria: A sculpture, incapable

00:11:06.240 --> 00:11:10.800
of moving while being watched, but would snap
the neck of the nearest conscious entity if

00:11:10.800 --> 00:11:16.000
left unobserved for even a fraction of a second.
Its relatively minimal killing left it easy

00:11:16.000 --> 00:11:20.960
to contain without causing mass deaths, and
despite all the other deaths that had sadly

00:11:20.960 --> 00:11:25.840
occurred during the KEY Project, Dr. Moto
believed that the lives saved in the long

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:30.240
run by stopping the Black Moon’s howls would
justify the sacrifice.

00:11:30.240 --> 00:11:34.800
The problem is...the KEY Project didn’t
stop anything.

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:39.600
Not long after this, there was the first recorded
double obliteration event in Rome, where a

00:11:39.600 --> 00:11:44.880
young tourist couple had both been obliterated
simultaneously. All the deaths in the KEY

00:11:44.880 --> 00:11:50.240
Project had been for nothing. The Black Moon
was only getting more powerful.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:55.200
The shame and the guilt was too much for Dr.
Moto. He left a note in his office, reading,

00:11:55.200 --> 00:12:00.000
“We've been looking at nothing. I'm sorry,
Administrator. I've failed you, sir.”

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:05.680
Moto’s corpse was later found in the sculpture’s
temporary containment chamber, his neck snapped.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:10.880
The KEY Project was, in summary, shut down
and its one surviving creation transported

00:12:10.880 --> 00:12:19.280
to Site-19 in late 1993, where it was designated
as SCP-173. Another painful failure for the

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:22.960
Administrator. Back to the drawing board once
more.

00:12:22.960 --> 00:12:26.960
Does the Black Moon howl? Not while stars
shine.

00:12:26.960 --> 00:12:32.080
millennia stretched on. Almost everyone died,
except The Administrator, thanks to his gift

00:12:32.080 --> 00:12:38.240
- or perhaps curse - as the Counterbalance
to the Black Moon. Science marched on, the

00:12:38.240 --> 00:12:41.600
SCP Foundation marched on, but all this progress,&nbsp;

00:12:42.160 --> 00:12:45.600
all this power, was nothing&nbsp;
against the incomprehensible

00:12:45.600 --> 00:12:52.240
influence of SCP-001. The Black Moon was howling
more frequently than ever, all the way up

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:58.160
to the year 3156, when the Foundation launched
the SEEK Project under the support of Project

00:12:58.160 --> 00:12:59.360
Oromasdes.

00:12:59.360 --> 00:13:04.080
As more and more people were wiped out in
frequent obliteration events, the Administrator

00:13:04.080 --> 00:13:08.960
became painfully aware that perhaps the answers
to the Black Moon problem wouldn’t be found

00:13:08.960 --> 00:13:13.920
on earth. Using state of the art technology,
with a little help from the anomalous, the

00:13:13.920 --> 00:13:18.880
SCP Foundation began work on an autonomous
space-faring vessel that could search the

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:26.240
stars for the key to the Black Moon’s destruction.
It was an awe-inspiring creation, a huge craft

00:13:26.240 --> 00:13:31.680
powered by artificial intelligence, with a
universal translator, cryogenic units, and

00:13:31.680 --> 00:13:35.600
hundreds of autonomous drones to perform more
targeted searches.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:40.640
SEEK was waved off into the unforgiving depths
of space. The Administrator could only hope

00:13:40.640 --> 00:13:43.680
that it would come back with worthwhile answers.

00:13:43.680 --> 00:13:48.240
The first of the three notable planets SEEK
arrived on was one theoretically capable of

00:13:48.240 --> 00:13:54.160
supporting human life, except for its brutal
and constant blizzards and snowstorms. When

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:59.280
SEEK’s drones were deployed, they did discover
signs of civilization, based around sentient

00:13:59.280 --> 00:14:04.880
spherical creatures, but no signs of actual
life remained. Records and statues found across

00:14:04.880 --> 00:14:08.880
the planet seemed to indicate that the Black
Moon was responsible for the destruction of

00:14:08.880 --> 00:14:14.000
the planet’s civilization, causing so many
obliteration events that the remaining survivors

00:14:14.000 --> 00:14:19.840
went mad from the fear and stress, leading
to mass death in the ensuing chaos.

00:14:19.840 --> 00:14:25.440
The next planet was discovered centuries later,
in the year 3499. While this planet could

00:14:25.440 --> 00:14:30.000
also theoretically support human life, it
suffered from frequent volcanic eruptions

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:34.720
that rendered much of its surface a flaming
mess. However, there were still the dormant

00:14:34.720 --> 00:14:40.320
ruins of a once advanced civilization of conscious
beings. Much like the prior planet, they’d

00:14:40.320 --> 00:14:45.840
been driven extinct by Black Moon obliteration
events a century before the SEEK even arrived.

00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:51.040
Unlike the last planet, however, it seems
that they accepted their fate, and went gently

00:14:51.040 --> 00:14:56.000
into the night. The planet was now overrun
by billions of armored, bat-like creatures

00:14:56.000 --> 00:15:00.960
that operated on pure instinct, and thus,
were not considered conscious enough to be

00:15:00.960 --> 00:15:02.000
obliterated.

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:08.560
The final planet was reached in 3764, and
was the most fruitful of the three discoveries.

00:15:08.560 --> 00:15:13.920
This planet was hyper-advanced, fully urbanized
and covered in sprawling megacities, with

00:15:13.920 --> 00:15:18.560
records and technology over a thousand years
ahead of Earth. Before the Black Moon killed

00:15:18.560 --> 00:15:23.520
almost all of them, they were a species of
humanoid telepathic fungi, and had developed

00:15:23.520 --> 00:15:28.080
an awareness of the Black Moon’s existence
that was on par with that of humanity’s.

00:15:28.080 --> 00:15:30.080
They even had their own equivalent of the&nbsp;

00:15:30.080 --> 00:15:33.440
SCP Foundation actively&nbsp;
working on countermeasures.

00:15:33.440 --> 00:15:38.960
And most amazingly of all, SEEK found one
surviving member of the species on the planet,

00:15:38.960 --> 00:15:44.000
cryogenically frozen. The craft was immediately
instructed to collect the survivor and return

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:48.320
home for interrogation. The Administrator
was preparing for what could have been the

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:54.000
most important conversation since he met the
Hermit, all those thousands of years ago.

00:15:54.000 --> 00:15:57.920
Does the Black Moon howl? Only when waning.

00:15:57.920 --> 00:16:02.960
When the surviving creature, codenamed SAGE,
was returned to Earth, The Administrator was

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:08.560
eager to finally speak with it. Like the rest
of its now-extinct species, SAGE spoke through

00:16:08.560 --> 00:16:13.280
powerful telepathic mindwaves, which only
The Administrator - thanks to his Counterbalance

00:16:13.280 --> 00:16:17.520
abilities - was able to receive at close range
without being harmed.

00:16:17.520 --> 00:16:21.920
Incidentally, it wasn’t long until the very
fact of the Administrator’s nature as a

00:16:21.920 --> 00:16:28.160
Counterbalance came up in the mental conversation.
SAGE could tell, just by being in his presence.

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:32.800
They discovered a number of vital truths over
their brief time communicating: That SAGE’s

00:16:32.800 --> 00:16:37.600
survival had been pure luck, for starters.
The Black Moon is still very much capable

00:16:37.600 --> 00:16:42.960
of obliterating conscious beings in an unconscious
state. The Administrator also learned that

00:16:42.960 --> 00:16:48.800
he was merely the latest in an extremely long
line of Counterbalances across time, space,

00:16:48.800 --> 00:16:54.480
and species, though everyone but him had waived
the duty, passed it on.

00:16:54.480 --> 00:17:01.680
SAGE had one question to ask the Administrator
in turn, “What is SCB?” The Singular Conceptual

00:17:01.680 --> 00:17:06.480
Bunker, being worked on and perfected for
thousands of years by now, by the Foundation’s

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:09.520
top scientists and conceptual engineers.

00:17:09.520 --> 00:17:12.400
The Administrator replied, “Victory. But&nbsp;

00:17:12.400 --> 00:17:16.480
it will take a very, very&nbsp;
long time.” Specifically,

00:17:16.480 --> 00:17:22.320
so long that he would see the stars go out
around him, one by one. Shocked, SAGE asked

00:17:22.320 --> 00:17:27.840
him what good victory would do him then. Rather
than say it aloud, he replied with a thought.

00:17:27.840 --> 00:17:33.360
SAGE paused, and said, “I see. How blasphemous
of you. Hopefully it works.”

00:17:33.360 --> 00:17:37.680
After this, the Administrator proceeded to
the Singular Conceptual Bunker and entered

00:17:37.680 --> 00:17:43.120
it, leaving instructions for the Foundation
to be run by a newly formed O5 Council in

00:17:43.120 --> 00:17:49.520
his indefinite absence. Thousands of years
later, in the year 5011, SAGE spoke one more

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:56.400
time, repeating the words, “Hopefully, hopefully”
before turning solid black, and disappearing.

00:17:56.400 --> 00:18:02.160
The Black Moon had claimed one more victim,
but billions more had gone in the interim.

00:18:02.160 --> 00:18:07.840
The Administrator had no more answers to give.
At least, no more answers that anyone but

00:18:07.840 --> 00:18:13.760
him would understand. He was inside the Singular
Conceptual Bunker now, loaded into a device

00:18:13.760 --> 00:18:20.080
known as TOME - an experimental memorial module,
meant to pick up and record all the last messages

00:18:20.080 --> 00:18:26.400
of every dying civilization across the universe,
when the time finally came. All he could do

00:18:26.400 --> 00:18:30.480
was wait. And wait was exactly what we did.

00:18:30.480 --> 00:18:32.160
Does the Black Moon howl?

00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.560
Yes. Yes it does.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:41.040
Years pass. Too many to count. It’s a time
after names now, and TOME sits in the very

00:18:41.040 --> 00:18:46.080
center, drinking in the end of the universe.
The last of all the human colonies across

00:18:46.080 --> 00:18:53.200
the universe were obliterated by the Black
Moon back in the year 7329, so, so, so long

00:18:53.200 --> 00:18:59.840
ago, but some of the final messages of fear,
panic, and distress still echoed around the

00:18:59.840 --> 00:19:01.360
Administrator’s mind.

00:19:01.360 --> 00:19:07.120
"Hello, is there anyone here? We — we require
assistance! There's … it's … it's taking

00:19:07.120 --> 00:19:12.560
people every day! We need help! There's barely
anyone left! We need help! Hello? Hello?!"

00:19:13.120 --> 00:19:18.640
"Cabal 09:43! We have abandoned the false
flesh! We have abandoned the false flesh!

00:19:18.640 --> 00:19:26.000
The shepherds crook broken 'neath my knee!
Cabal 09:43! Cabal 09:43! Forgive us! Forgive

00:19:26.000 --> 00:19:26.400
us!"

00:19:26.960 --> 00:19:32.080
"We're going to leave this on. It's so dark
outside now. It's blotting out the sun. It's

00:19:32.080 --> 00:19:33.280
… I have to go now."

00:19:35.120 --> 00:19:35.920
"RESPOND•FIRST•CONVENIENCE&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:19:38.720 --> 00:19:42.480
EMERGENCY•SITUATION•DEVELOPING
REQUIRE•ADDITIONAL•RESOURCES."

00:19:42.480 --> 00:19:47.360
"My fault. Your fault. Our fault. My fault.
Your fault. Our fault. My fault. Your fault.

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:50.720
Our fault. Rip out my brain now. Rip out my
brain now!"

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:58.080
And a small child, the last on Earth, simply
asking, “Hello?” into an indifferent microphone.

00:19:58.080 --> 00:20:04.000
But the Administrator had to wait, as the
Singular Conceptual Bunker became the Solitary

00:20:04.000 --> 00:20:09.600
Conceptual Bunker. He was the last conscious
being in the universe, and still, he needed

00:20:09.600 --> 00:20:15.920
to wait, as the stars went dark outside. Only
when there was nothing outside but black was

00:20:15.920 --> 00:20:20.240
it finally time for the Counterbalance’s
long game to pay off.

00:20:20.240 --> 00:20:25.840
There was nothing left of our universe. The
only thing here was the SCB, and the Black

00:20:25.840 --> 00:20:31.440
Moon itself. With everything else gone, the
Black Moon only had one conscious being left

00:20:31.440 --> 00:20:37.440
to obliterate. It opened the door to the Solitary
Conceptual Bunker, and stepped inside.

00:20:37.440 --> 00:20:44.080
This...this doesn’t make sense. How can
the Black Moon, an entity beyond our dimension,

00:20:44.080 --> 00:20:50.880
beyond physical form, take a step? Good question.
The same question, incidentally, that was

00:20:50.880 --> 00:20:55.440
going through the Black Moon’s mind as it
entered the bunker. It didn’t look at all

00:20:55.440 --> 00:21:01.600
how the entity expected: It was like a bar,
a counter with rows of bottles behind it,

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:06.960
a jukebox playing in the corner. A man stood
behind the bar, cleaning glasses.

00:21:06.960 --> 00:21:10.480
The Counterbalance. The Administrator.

00:21:10.480 --> 00:21:16.240
He said, "Well, there you are! Certainly took
your time. Can I pour you a little something?"

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:22.320
This only served to increase the Black Moon’s
confusion. It had form here, dark smoke compressed

00:21:22.320 --> 00:21:30.000
into a vaguely humanoid shape. It could speak?
It could think? None of this made any sense.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:34.640
The being that’d just wiped out all conscious
life and seen the very death of the universe

00:21:34.640 --> 00:21:37.840
was truly and utterly confused.

00:21:37.840 --> 00:21:42.720
The Administrator just seemed to be enjoying
himself, preparing for a confrontation hundreds

00:21:42.720 --> 00:21:48.320
of billions of years in the making. The Singular
Conceptual Bunker - or perhaps, the Singular

00:21:48.320 --> 00:21:55.200
Containment Bunker - was a truly ingenious
creation. A place of pure ideas, where everything

00:21:55.200 --> 00:22:02.720
inside was on the same level. Here, there
were no immortals. No Gods. Just ideas, on

00:22:02.720 --> 00:22:08.960
the same level playing field. And it was time
for the Black Moon’s idea to come to an

00:22:08.960 --> 00:22:09.600
end.

00:22:09.600 --> 00:22:13.440
It was a trap, and the entire universe was
the bait.

00:22:13.440 --> 00:22:17.440
Without warning, the Administrator pulled
up a shotgun from underneath the table, and

00:22:17.440 --> 00:22:20.480
unleashed both barrels into the Black Moon’s
chest.

00:22:20.480 --> 00:22:24.560
The creature took the hit and fought back,
dragging the Administrator to the ground,

00:22:24.560 --> 00:22:29.600
beating him, strangling him. He could feel
the light fading under the monster’s relentless

00:22:29.600 --> 00:22:34.960
assault, until he managed to get his desperate
hands on a glass ashtray. He beat the monster

00:22:34.960 --> 00:22:39.440
over the head with it until its grip loosened,
and he was able to slide out.

00:22:39.440 --> 00:22:43.920
There, the killer of the universe was on the
ground before him. He grabbed the monster,

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:49.200
held it in place, and beat it to death. He
was gravely injured by the battle, but The

00:22:49.200 --> 00:22:55.920
Black Moon was no more. Here, in the Singular
Conceptual Bunker, he had won.

00:22:55.920 --> 00:23:00.400
The Administrator, no longer the counterbalance
in the absence of the Black Moon, hobbled

00:23:00.400 --> 00:23:06.160
over to the jukebox, producing a single, beautiful
coin from his pocket. He pushed the coin into

00:23:06.160 --> 00:23:09.360
the slot, wheezed a pained breath, and said:

00:23:09.360 --> 00:23:17.680
“The thing is … this place is only information.
T-There's nothing else out there. Not even

00:23:17.680 --> 00:23:24.000
matter. The universe closed its doors a long
time ago. But this place can go from information

00:23:24.000 --> 00:23:30.160
back to matter with just the press of a button.
L-Let's see what happens when we introduce

00:23:30.160 --> 00:23:32.000
something to nothing…”

00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:37.120
For a second, it looks as though he might
fall, but he doesn’t. Instead, he slams

00:23:37.120 --> 00:23:42.960
the button on the jukebox and, with a relieved
laugh, says, “Let there be light.”

00:23:42.960 --> 00:23:45.360
And there was light.

00:23:45.360 --> 00:23:53.680
Now go check out “SCP-001 - Which is the
Real 001?” and “SCP-001 EX - A Good Boy”

00:23:53.680 --> 00:23:58.960
to unravel more of the many mysteries of the
legendary SCP-001!

